{"id":"cybersecurity-careers","title":"Careers in cybersecurity","subject":"Cybersecurity","label":"Cybersecurity","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":185,"duration":185.44,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":466,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":15.875},{"id":"explain","title":"Roles and teams","start":15.875,"end":54.655},{"id":"explain2","title":"Skills and certs","start":54.655,"end":87.085},{"id":"example","title":"Six month plan","start":87.085,"end":121.895},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":121.895,"end":128.035},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":128.035,"end":135.525},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":135.525,"end":153.595},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":153.595,"end":185.44}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.54,"text":"Your bank blocks a strange payment at two in the morning. Someone noticed.","w":[0.54,0.76,1.08,1.46,1.56,2,2.4,2.52,2.76,2.84,2.94,3.74,4.06]},{"s":0,"a":4.84,"b":8.9,"text":"Who? I'm Kora, and today we look at careers in cybersecurity.","w":[4.9,5.6,5.78,6.56,6.68,7.08,7.2,7.4,7.5,8,8.1]},{"s":0,"a":9.2,"b":15.45,"text":"The roles, the certificates, and how you can start for free, even with just a laptop and a little data.","w":[9.24,9.38,10.2,10.34,11.52,11.68,11.88,12,12.18,12.5,12.7,13.46,13.68,13.84,14.08,14.16,14.7,14.82,14.88,15.1]},{"s":1,"a":16.3,"b":22.27,"text":"There's a worldwide shortage of security people, so the work is in demand, and much of it can be done from anywhere.","w":[16.32,16.58,16.66,17.32,17.7,17.82,18.32,19.16,19.3,19.44,19.74,19.86,19.98,20.72,20.86,21.08,21.18,21.28,21.44,21.56,21.78,21.96]},{"s":1,"a":22.57,"b":27.94,"text":"A security analyst in a security operations centre watches for alerts and investigates them.","w":[22.64,22.72,23.3,23.86,23.96,24.06,24.62,25.22,25.86,26.3,26.48,27.02,27.16,27.76]},{"s":1,"a":28.24,"b":31.54,"text":"A penetration tester is paid to test defences, with permission.","w":[28.32,28.4,29.04,29.42,29.56,29.88,29.98,30.22,30.88,31.08]},{"s":1,"a":31.84,"b":34,"text":"An incident responder handles a breach.","w":[31.88,32.1,32.5,33.1,33.5,33.6]},{"s":1,"a":34.3,"b":37.28,"text":"A security engineer builds and maintains defences.","w":[34.38,34.48,35.06,35.5,35.94,36.06,36.64]},{"s":1,"a":37.58,"b":42.28,"text":"Governance, risk and compliance writes policy and checks the rules are followed.","w":[37.62,38.56,38.96,39.08,39.64,39.92,40.78,41,41.32,41.44,41.74,41.86]},{"s":1,"a":42.58,"b":45.06,"text":"Digital forensics investigates what happened.","w":[42.58,43.02,43.72,44.44,44.64]},{"s":1,"a":45.36,"b":49.44,"text":"Together, these roles cover preventing, detecting and responding to threats.","w":[45.36,45.82,46.14,46.5,46.82,47.58,48.2,48.32,48.84,48.96]},{"s":1,"a":49.74,"b":54.23,"text":"Blue team defends. Red team tests by attacking, always with permission.","w":[49.78,50.06,50.3,51.28,51.52,51.8,52.18,52.38,53.26,53.6,53.78]},{"s":2,"a":55.08,"b":64.18,"text":"Skills come first: networking, operating systems, especially Linux, a scripting language such as Python, and clear writing, because every finding becomes a report.","w":[55.18,55.58,55.82,56.64,57.44,57.94,58.46,59.04,59.7,59.76,60.18,60.6,60.82,60.96,61.54,61.7,61.96,62.28,62.68,62.96,63.32,63.66,63.72]},{"s":2,"a":64.48,"b":73.87,"text":"Entry certificates people commonly start with are CompTIA Security Plus, the I S C two Certified in Cybersecurity, and Google's cybersecurity certificate.","w":[64.56,64.92,65.94,66.3,66.74,67.02,67.36,67.52,68.12,68.58,69.26,69.58,69.84,69.96,70.18,70.44,70.96,71.08,72.2,72.34,72.72,73.42]},{"s":2,"a":74.17,"b":78.8,"text":"Later ones include CEH, OSCP and CISSP.","w":[74.24,74.6,74.82,75.62,76.7,77.66,77.84]},{"s":2,"a":79.1,"b":83.88,"text":"Each certificate shows employers what you can do, but the skills underneath matter more.","w":[79.14,79.34,79.92,80.2,80.7,80.86,80.98,81.14,81.94,82.1,82.28,82.74,83.22,83.52]},{"s":2,"a":84.18,"b":86.66,"text":"A degree helps, but it is not the only route.","w":[84.24,84.32,84.7,85.4,85.54,85.66,85.8,86,86.2,86.44]},{"s":3,"a":87.51,"b":91.27,"text":"Here's a plan for your first six months, with a laptop and limited data.","w":[87.54,87.84,87.92,88.2,88.32,88.5,88.76,89.04,89.58,89.76,89.84,90.42,90.58,90.94]},{"s":3,"a":91.57,"b":95.8,"text":"Month one. Learn networking and Linux basics from free written guides.","w":[91.64,92.04,92.72,93.02,93.6,93.74,94.08,94.52,94.78,95.02,95.3]},{"s":3,"a":96.1,"b":101.02,"text":"Month two. Start a scripting language, Python, and write short notes on what you learn.","w":[96.18,96.52,97.4,97.78,97.86,98.3,98.78,99.38,99.52,99.8,100.06,100.32,100.44,100.58,100.72]},{"s":3,"a":101.32,"b":105.02,"text":"Month three. Build a small home lab on your own machine only.","w":[101.42,101.74,102.56,102.86,102.94,103.28,103.52,103.82,103.9,104.1,104.26,104.72]},{"s":3,"a":105.32,"b":109.43,"text":"Month four. Join legal capture the flag competitions and free practice labs.","w":[105.4,105.7,106.16,106.5,106.8,107.16,107.28,107.58,108.22,108.36,108.6,109]},{"s":3,"a":109.73,"b":115.17,"text":"Month five. Write up each exercise as a short report, in clear English.","w":[109.82,110.2,111.2,111.54,111.76,112.04,112.72,112.84,112.98,113.28,114.12,114.32,114.74]},{"s":3,"a":115.47,"b":121.47,"text":"Month six. Pick one entry certificate, study for it, and join a community to ask questions.","w":[115.56,115.88,116.72,117.06,117.28,117.58,118.52,118.84,119.08,119.52,119.64,119.9,119.96,120.46,120.64,120.84]},{"s":4,"a":122.32,"b":125.15,"text":"Quick check. Which team defends, blue or red?","w":[122.36,122.64,123.34,123.62,123.86,124.36,124.7,124.86]},{"s":4,"a":125.6,"b":127.61,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[125.62,125.92,126.2,126.34,126.6,127.1,127.28]},{"s":5,"a":128.46,"b":129.46,"text":"Blue team defends.","w":[128.48,128.82,129.1]},{"s":5,"a":129.76,"b":135.1,"text":"Red team tests defences by attacking with permission, so the defenders are blue, not red.","w":[129.84,130.1,130.4,130.82,131.38,131.58,131.98,132.14,132.94,133.1,133.2,133.66,133.8,134.6,134.82]},{"s":6,"a":135.95,"b":137.31,"text":"Three common mistakes.","w":[136.02,136.38,136.74]},{"s":6,"a":137.61,"b":142.06,"text":"First, touching systems without permission. That is illegal, and it ends careers.","w":[137.62,138.12,138.5,138.88,139.18,140.16,140.42,140.62,141.14,141.26,141.36,141.56]},{"s":6,"a":142.36,"b":146.92,"text":"Second, chasing certificates before skills. Learn the basics first.","w":[142.46,143.34,143.8,144.42,144.78,145.66,145.92,146.04,146.5]},{"s":6,"a":147.22,"b":153.17,"text":"Third, skipping the writing. Every finding becomes a report, so practise clear writing.","w":[147.3,148.08,148.44,148.54,149.6,149.9,150.32,150.72,150.8,151.76,151.96,152.48,152.78]},{"s":7,"a":154.02,"b":160.34,"text":"Recap. One: security has a worldwide shortage of people, and the work can be done from anywhere in the world.","w":[154.08,154.7,155.68,156.26,156.44,156.52,157.12,157.48,157.6,158.26,158.38,158.5,158.74,158.88,158.98,159.2,159.46,159.82,159.9,160]},{"s":7,"a":160.64,"b":166.96,"text":"Two: blue team defends, red team tests with permission, and roles range from analyst to forensics.","w":[160.66,161.38,161.68,161.92,162.74,162.96,163.22,163.62,163.8,164.64,164.82,165.16,165.48,165.76,166.14,166.26]},{"s":7,"a":167.26,"b":175.88,"text":"Three: skills come first, then entry certificates like CompTIA Security Plus, the I S C two Certified in Cybersecurity or Google's certificate.","w":[167.34,168.18,168.54,168.78,169.6,169.96,170.24,170.84,171.04,171.52,171.94,172.64,172.92,173.18,173.28,173.5,173.76,174.22,174.32,174.98,175.1,175.42]},{"s":7,"a":176.18,"b":181.38,"text":"Top tip: write up everything you practise, because clear writing turns practice into proof of skill.","w":[176.2,176.48,177.04,177.3,177.52,177.86,178.02,178.76,179.1,179.38,179.7,179.98,180.48,180.7,180.96,181.08]},{"s":7,"a":181.68,"b":184.84,"text":"Keep learning with Knowzone, and I'll see you in the next lesson.","w":[181.7,181.98,182.3,182.48,183.4,183.52,183.72,183.9,184.04,184.12,184.24,184.48]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Careers in cybersecurity","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Bank blocks strange payment at 2am"},{"at":4.74,"kind":"text","text":"Kora: careers in cybersecurity"},{"at":9.1,"kind":"text","text":"Roles, certificates, free start: laptop + data"}]},{"at":16.05,"heading":"Roles in security","items":[{"at":16.2,"kind":"text","text":"Worldwide shortage; work from anywhere"},{"at":22.47,"kind":"term","text":"Security analyst","detail":"Watches alerts in a security operations centre"},{"at":28.14,"kind":"term","text":"Penetration tester","detail":"Tests defences with permission"},{"at":31.74,"kind":"term","text":"Incident responder","detail":"Handles a breach"},{"at":34.2,"kind":"term","text":"Security engineer","detail":"Builds and maintains defences"}]},{"at":37.33,"heading":"More roles & teams","items":[{"at":37.48,"kind":"term","text":"GRC","detail":"Governance, risk & compliance: policy and rules"},{"at":42.48,"kind":"term","text":"Digital forensics","detail":"Investigates what happened"},{"at":45.26,"kind":"text","text":"Roles cover prevent, detect, respond"},{"at":49.64,"kind":"term","text":"Blue team / Red team","detail":"Blue defends; red tests by attacking with permission"}]},{"at":54.83,"heading":"Skills & certificates","items":[{"at":54.98,"kind":"term","text":"Core skills","detail":"Networking, OS (esp. Linux), scripting (Python), clear writing"},{"at":64.38,"kind":"term","text":"Entry certificates","detail":"CompTIA Security+, ISC2 Certified in Cybersecurity, Google cert"},{"at":74.07,"kind":"term","text":"Later certificates","detail":"CEH, OSCP, CISSP"},{"at":79,"kind":"text","text":"Certs show ability; skills matter more"},{"at":84.08,"kind":"text","text":"Degree helps, but not the only route"}]},{"at":87.26,"heading":"Six-month plan: 1–3","items":[{"at":87.41,"kind":"text","text":"Laptop + limited data"},{"at":91.47,"kind":"text","text":"Month 1: networking + Linux basics (free guides)"},{"at":96,"kind":"text","text":"Month 2: Python + short notes"},{"at":101.22,"kind":"text","text":"Month 3: small home lab on own machine only"}]},{"at":105.07,"heading":"Six-month plan: 4–6","items":[{"at":105.22,"kind":"text","text":"Month 4: legal capture-the-flag + free labs"},{"at":109.63,"kind":"text","text":"Month 5: write each exercise as a short report"},{"at":115.37,"kind":"text","text":"Month 6: pick one entry cert, study, join community"}]},{"at":121.89,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":121.89,"kind":"question","text":"Which team defends, blue or red?"}]},{"at":128.21,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":128.36,"kind":"text","text":"Blue team defends."},{"at":129.66,"kind":"text","text":"Red tests by attacking with permission; defenders are blue"}]},{"at":135.7,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":135.85,"kind":"text","text":"Three common mistakes"},{"at":137.51,"kind":"wrong","text":"Touching systems without permission"},{"at":142.26,"kind":"wrong","text":"Chasing certificates before skills"},{"at":147.12,"kind":"wrong","text":"Skipping the writing"}]},{"at":153.77,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":153.92,"kind":"text","text":"Worldwide shortage; work from anywhere"},{"at":160.54,"kind":"text","text":"Blue defends; red tests with permission"},{"at":167.16,"kind":"text","text":"Skills first; then entry certs (Security+, ISC2 CC, Google)"},{"at":176.08,"kind":"tip","text":"Write up all you practise: clear writing turns practice into proof of skill."}]}],"check":{"at":127.86,"seconds":10,"question":"Which team defends, blue or red?","answer":"Blue team defends."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}